+## October 16, 2026: water and shoreline
+
+No hard line where the water meets anything, engine-wide. Found: the sea's ground eased the island's floor into the Bay Area survey (13 m down under the island) across a band that began 100 m inside the island's centre, so every beach was drawn 5 to 8 m deep (opaque turquoise to the sand, the full swell on the beach); and the depth, the swash and the edge were worked out at the sea's vertices (3 to 7 m apart near you), so every contour was a straight line and a vertex's swash filled whole triangles on the sand. Now the island's beaches keep their own depths, and out to 520 m (160 on a phone) every pixel reads the ground under it: the water's cover fades with its true depth to nothing at the edge (the real wet sand shows through, tinted turquoise by red-first absorption), colour runs continuously from beach to deep. A shared shore module (`world/shore.js`, also driving the wet sand in `terrain.js`) gives the swash a rush, a stall and a drain that gathers pace, and a front broken into lobes and fingers drawn anew each wave; the sheet thins to nothing, a frothing bore at its front, lace carried down in the backwash, bubbles popping, a line of lace left on the sand that breaks up; the sand stays dark where the water ran and dries slowly, glossy only for a few seconds. Breakers (crest pitching forward, white water rolling in) on gentle open beaches only; none on steep or sheltered shores. Steep shores are wet dark rock from the waterline to the spray's reach, the surf bursts white on them and throws spray (`spray.js`, also the pier's posts). Posts, the boat and you wading ring the water with ripples and foam; rain pocks it; streams running into the sea spread a silty plume with a current line (`bay/water.js mouths`); Snell's window from below; the nearest lamps lie in the water at night and foam no longer glows. Lakes lap, creek edges creep, lava margins crust with glowing break-outs; a toxic sea's foam is scum. A planet's lakes and streams are mapped (`island.waterMap`, `shared.uWaterMap`): silt on the bed, wet mud banks, and the grass kept out of the water (one line in `grass.js`; `WATERMAP_GLSL` for the land agent). Phones: shorter per-pixel reach, less foam detail by tier, no depth pre-pass, no per-frame allocation. One line in `main.js` (`ocean.userData.tick`). Tests: `island/tools/shore.test.mjs`. See `docs/water-shoreline-2026-10-16.md`.
+
 ## October 15, 2026: mobile controls
 
 The touch HUD has one look and one layout in portrait and landscape: round, semi-transparent buttons with a white line glyph and no words under or inside them (`island/src/ui/touch-skin.js`, applied once from `main.js` on touch screens only). Glyphs are inline SVG masks matched to each button by its name (anything unknown gets a pointing-hand glyph, never words; changing captions such as Takedown, Swing or Slash are glyph swaps); every button keeps its `aria-label` (one without is named from its words) and a title. By thumb, inside the safe areas: the primary action bottom right (Fire, Strike, the pedal, the cast) at 68 px with Aim/Block/brake, Reload/Dodge/a vehicle's gun, Mode/Grab and Surrender round it at 52 px; jump and the context buttons (leave the car, the boat, the rod, which car, assist, camera) in a column above; the stick, or steering (and an aircraft's Up and Down), bottom left; things to act on nearby in a row between the thumbs; back, home and the folded contract top left; fly, gear, places, the menu, music and settings in one row top right; tips under the top row. Driving, melee, boats and fishing only show their own controls; the drive button comes out of the menu as an exit while you drive. The quest chip has its own band and nothing sits on it (measured at run time, with Safari's bars read from the visual viewport). Looking round (`ui/touch-look.js`): a floating stick in the lower left, free look anywhere else with both thumbs at once, an acceleration curve, invert up and down and gyro aiming in Sky and World, and the view easing back to level as you walk. Control tips on a phone show once (`firstTime`). Desktop unchanged apart from tooltips. Tests: `island/tools/touch-skin.test.mjs`, `island/tools/mobile-controls-browser.cjs` (now with the skin). See `docs/mobile-controls-2026-10-15.md`.
